<main class="lp-page" id="lead-provider-guide">
  <div class="lp-hero-shell">
    <div class="lp-wrap">
      <nav class="lp-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/resources/outbound-sales-library/">Outbound Sales Library</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">B2B lead providers</span></nav>
      <div class="lp-hero">
        <div>
          <p class="lp-kicker">The CallTeam buying desk</p>
          <h1>Best B2B <span>lead generation databases.</span><small>10 providers. CallTeam’s verdict.</small></h1>
          <p class="lp-lede">Apollo, ZoomInfo, Cognism, UpLead, Lusha, Lead411, RocketReach, SalesIntel, Seamless.AI and AeroLeads.</p>
          <p class="lp-intro">Where to buy leads. What each provider does well. What we do not like. The checks that could save you a bad purchase.</p>
          <div class="lp-actions"><a class="lp-button" href="#comparison">Compare all 10 databases <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="lp-text-link" href="#test-plan">Get the free test scorecard ↗</a></div>
        </div>
        <aside class="lp-brief" aria-labelledby="lp-brief-title">
          <p class="lp-kicker">Before you buy another list</p>
          <h2 id="lp-brief-title">100 contacts.<br>How many can you actually use?</h2>
          <ol><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Right company. Right person.</strong><p>Does the record fit the job you sell?</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><strong>A route to reach them.</strong><p>Mobile, direct line or company number?</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><strong>A cost you can explain.</strong><p>Count useful contacts after the checks.</p></div></li></ol>
          <a href="#cost-check">Work out your cost per usable contact →</a>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <p class="lp-direct-answer"><strong>Our starting shortlist:</strong> Apollo for data and outreach together. UpLead for a clear contact-credit model. AeroLeads for one-time purchases. Cognism and SalesIntel when phone data and verification deserve a closer test. ZoomInfo when several teams need a broader platform. Choose by the work you need done, then test your actual buyers.</p>
      <p class="lp-method"><strong>Sources checked {{ guide.reviewed }}.</strong> CallTeam uses Apollo and lists it as a technology partner. We have not run a controlled ten-provider benchmark. Product details come from the official sources linked below; the verdicts are our assessment. Provider links go directly to their websites or official announcements.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="lp-jump" aria-label="On this page"><div class="lp-wrap"><a href="#comparison">Quick comparison</a><a href="#provider-verdicts">Our verdicts</a><a href="#compare-two">Compare two</a><a href="#test-plan">Free scorecard</a><a href="#cost-check">Cost calculator</a><a href="#questions">Questions</a></div></nav>

  <section class="lp-section" id="comparison"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">01 / Make your shortlist</p><h2>10 B2B lead databases.<br>Which fits your sales team?</h2><p>A lead generation database lets you find companies and people by criteria such as role, industry and location. Buying their contact details gives you a prospecting list. It does not mean those people have asked to hear from you.</p></div>
    <div class="lp-database-criteria"><h3>How we judge the shortlist</h3><p>Five checks: coverage of your target accounts, the contact fields you need, the full cost per usable contact, how the data reaches your CRM, and what “verified” actually means. Our verdicts weigh the buying workflow and published terms. Your sample establishes whether the data fits.</p></div>
    <p class="lp-scroll-hint">On a small screen, swipe the table to see every column.</p>
    <div class="lp-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="lp-table-caption"><table class="lp-table"><caption id="lp-table-caption">10 lead generation databases compared: use cases, billing and buying checks</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">Worth considering when</th><th scope="col">How you pay</th><th scope="col">The catch to check</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for p in guide.providers %}<tr><th scope="row"><a href="#{{ p.id }}">{{ p.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></th><td>{{ p.fit }}</td><td>{{ p.billing }}</td><td>{{ p.catch }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
    <p class="lp-small">This is a shortlist, not a ranking. Plan terms change. Use the official sources in each review and confirm currency, billing period and the total commitment in your quote.</p>
    <div class="lp-note"><strong>Do not compare credits as if they are the same currency.</strong><p>A credit might unlock a contact, reveal a phone or move a record into your CRM. Ask what you will spend to finish the job.</p></div>
    <p class="lp-small"><strong>Data chosen? Price the calling setup.</strong> Compare the <a href="/resources/best-cold-calling-dialers/">10 best cold calling diallers</a>, including plan limits, a cost calculator and a free trial kit.</p>
    <p class="lp-small"><strong>Next: choose what to buy.</strong> Use our <a href="/resources/how-to-buy-cold-calling-leads/">mobile vs company numbers guide</a> to choose a calling route, handle voicemail and AI screening, and get a free calling-list template.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="provider-verdicts"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">02 / The useful differences</p><h2>Ten providers.<br>Ten honest verdicts.</h2><p>Published features are one thing. Whether they help your campaign is the test.</p></div>
    <div class="lp-provider-nav" aria-label="Jump to a provider">{% for p in guide.providers %}<a href="#{{ p.id }}">{{ p.name }}</a>{% endfor %}</div>
    {% for p in guide.providers %}<article class="lp-provider" id="{{ p.id }}" aria-labelledby="{{ p.id }}-title">
      <div class="lp-provider-head"><div><p class="lp-kicker">{{ p.tag }}</p><h3 id="{{ p.id }}-title">{{ p.name }}</h3></div><a class="lp-source" href="{{ p.sources[0].url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ p.sourceAction or 'Check current plans' }} ↗</a></div>
      <div class="lp-provider-body"><div class="lp-provider-detail"><h4>What it is good at</h4><p>{{ p.strength }}</p><h4>What we do not like</h4><p>{{ p.drawback }}</p><h4>What we still do not know</h4><p>{{ p.unknown }}</p></div><aside class="lp-verdict"><p class="lp-kicker">CallTeam verdict</p><p class="lp-verdict-text">{{ p.verdict }}</p><div><strong>Before you buy</strong><p>{{ p.check }}</p></div></aside></div>
      {% if p.id == "zoominfo" %}<p class="lp-small"><strong>Reviewing a ZoomInfo quote or renewal?</strong> Compare <a href="/resources/zoominfo-alternatives/">ZoomInfo alternatives for small sales teams</a>, including published prices, phone access and the full commitment.</p>{% endif %}
      {% if p.id == "apollo" %}<p class="lp-small"><strong>Already using Apollo?</strong> Compare <a href="/resources/apollo-alternatives/">Apollo alternatives for cold calling</a> and decide whether to keep it, add another data source or replace it.</p>{% endif %}
      <p class="lp-sources"><strong>Official sources:</strong> {% for source in p.sources %}<a href="{{ source.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ source.label }} ↗</a>{% if not loop.last %}<span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
    </article>{% endfor %}
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section" id="compare-two"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">03 / Down to two?</p><h2>Compare your finalists.</h2><p>Choose two names to put the buying checks next to each other.</p></div>
    <p class="lp-small">Considering LinkedIn for prospecting? Our <a href="/resources/linkedin-sales-navigator-lead-generation/">Sales Navigator vs Apollo guide</a> compares buyer research, contact access and the steps needed before calling.</p>
    <div class="lp-js-only" hidden>
      <div class="lp-selectors"><div><label for="lp-left">First provider</label><select id="lp-left">{% for p in guide.providers %}<option value="{{ p.id }}"{% if p.id == 'apollo' %} selected{% endif %}>{{ p.name }}</option>{% endfor %}</select></div><div><label for="lp-right">Second provider</label><select id="lp-right">{% for p in guide.providers %}<option value="{{ p.id }}"{% if p.id == 'zoominfo' %} selected{% endif %}>{{ p.name }}</option>{% endfor %}</select></div></div>
      <p class="lp-small" id="lp-selection-status" role="status"></p><div class="lp-pair" id="lp-pair"></div>
    </div>
    <noscript><p>The full comparison and all ten reviews above work without JavaScript.</p></noscript>
    <div class="lp-matchups">
      <div><h3>Apollo vs ZoomInfo</h3><p>Is your problem finding and contacting prospects, or coordinating several teams and data workflows? Price the work you will actually use, then compare the same sample. Platform breadth does not establish better phone data.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Apollo vs Cognism</h3><p>If mobiles are the reason you are shopping, compare usable mobile coverage for the same roles and territory. Check the verification status and cost of those specific records before paying for a premium package.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Apollo vs UpLead</h3><p>Decide whether you need outreach software alongside the data. If your CRM and dialler are already working, compare the cost and effort of adding useful contacts to them.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Lusha vs Lead411</h3><p>Translate reveal charges and export allowances into the same finished task: usable records in your CRM. Test both on the same accounts. The largest allowance is not necessarily the best purchase.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Apollo vs AeroLeads</h3><p>Do you need a continuing prospecting and outreach platform, or a focused data purchase? AeroLeads offers one-time credit packs. Compare the contacts you can actually use, including phone charges, before choosing by subscription price alone.</p></div>
      <div><h3>SalesIntel vs RocketReach</h3><p>Compare the verification information attached to each sample. SalesIntel separates human, email and machine verification; RocketReach describes phone confidence grades and number-type filters. Those labels mean different things. Check the person and number behind them.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-dark" id="test-plan"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">04 / Free. No email required.</p><h2>Give every provider<br>the same test.</h2><p>Use the scorecard to compare a small working sample. No random demo contacts. No cherry-picked success stories.</p></div>
    <ol class="lp-test-steps"><li><strong>Choose the accounts yourself.</strong><p>Start with 50 target companies as a practical pilot, not a statistically conclusive benchmark. Specify the same geography, company fit and buying roles. Record accounts each provider cannot cover.</p></li><li><strong>Inspect before importing.</strong><p>Check the company, current role, number type and duplicate people. Separate a missing phone from a wrong phone. Flag shared company numbers so two reps do not call the same switchboard at once.</p></li><li><strong>Work a controlled batch.</strong><p>Keep the offer, caller, attempt policy and calling windows comparable. Do not call the same person twice to test two suppliers. Mark overlapping records and avoid double-counting outcomes.</p></li><li><strong>Buy the next batch from the evidence.</strong><p>Record useful conversations and held meetings separately from data quality. An unanswered call is not proof of a bad number. Small samples give direction; they do not establish a universal winner.</p></li></ol>
    <div class="lp-download-row"><div><h3>A scorecard for all ten providers.</h3><p>Account coverage, phone types, wrong numbers, duplicates, usable contacts, cost and sales outcomes.</p></div><div><a class="lp-button" href="/assets/downloads/b2b-lead-provider-test-scorecard.csv" download="CallTeam-Lead-Provider-Test-Scorecard.csv">Download the free CSV <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><p class="lp-small">Blank comparison template for Excel or Google Sheets. The website calculator does the maths.</p></div></div>
    <details class="lp-supplier-questions"><summary>Questions to send the supplier</summary><div id="lp-supplier-copy"><p>Can you show coverage for these accounts and roles, with missing records included?</p><p>Which numbers are mobile, work direct or company HQ? What was verified, and when?</p><p>What will we pay to reveal, enrich and export this batch? What costs extra?</p><p>What happens with wrong records, unused credits, renewal, cancellation and downloaded data after cancellation?</p></div><button class="lp-button lp-js-only" id="lp-copy" type="button" hidden>Copy these questions</button><span id="lp-copy-status" role="status"></span></details>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section" id="cost-check"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">05 / Make the maths honest</p><h2>What does a usable<br>contact actually cost?</h2><p>Define usable before comparing: a unique person at a suitable company, in the right role, with the contact route your campaign requires. Remove suppressed contacts. A phone label alone is not a completed quality check.</p></div>
    <div class="lp-calculator lp-js-only" hidden><form id="lp-cost-form" action="#cost-check" method="get" novalidate><p class="lp-small">Illustrative starting values. Replace them with your sample results.</p><div class="lp-input-grid"><div><label for="lp-currency">Currency</label><select id="lp-currency"><option value="USD">USD</option><option value="CAD">CAD</option><option value="GBP">GBP</option><option value="EUR">EUR</option></select></div><div><label for="lp-cost">Data cost for this sample</label><input id="lp-cost" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal" value="100" required></div><div><label for="lp-exported">Contacts exported</label><input id="lp-exported" type="number" min="1" step="1" inputmode="numeric" value="50" required></div><div><label for="lp-usable">Usable unique contacts</label><input id="lp-usable" type="number" min="0" step="1" inputmode="numeric" value="35" required></div></div><p class="lp-small" id="lp-cost-help">Allocate subscription and seat costs to the same sample period. Add reveals, exports and extra enrichment. This is data cost, excluding rep time and dialler costs. Currency selection labels your inputs; it does not convert them.</p><button class="lp-button" type="submit">Calculate my contact cost →</button><p id="lp-cost-error" class="lp-error" role="alert"></p></form><div class="lp-result" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"><span>Cost per usable contact</span><strong id="lp-cost-result">USD 2.86</strong><p id="lp-yield-result">35 of 50 contacts usable · 70%</p><p id="lp-result-note">Data cost ÷ usable unique contacts. A usable contact is not a meeting or a customer.</p></div></div>
    <noscript><p><strong>Formula:</strong> sample data cost ÷ usable unique contacts. For example, a $100 sample with 35 usable contacts costs $2.86 per usable contact. If none are usable, report no usable contacts rather than a zero cost.</p></noscript>
    <div class="lp-field-note"><p class="lp-kicker">A calling decision you will recognise</p><h3>Out of mobiles. Still have company numbers.</h3><p>Your first mobile pass is finished. There are still relevant accounts with company numbers in the CRM. That does not automatically mean you need 200 new contacts.</p><p>Split the queue into mobile, work direct, company number and missing phone. Keep callbacks and do-not-call records out of the retry queue. Test the unworked company numbers where the account fit is strong, then use the gaps to decide what to buy.</p><p>For the next purchase, use the sectors, locations and roles that produced useful conversations. Buy missing coverage. Do not pay twice for the same company and call it growth.</p><a class="lp-text-link" href="/articles/b2b-prospect-list-building-services/">See what a usable prospect list needs →</a></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="questions"><div class="lp-wrap lp-faq-wrap"><div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">06 / Before you commit</p><h2>Questions sales teams ask<br>before buying leads.</h2></div><div class="lp-faqs">{% for faq in guide.faqs %}<details><summary>{{ faq.q }}</summary><p>{{ faq.a }}</p></details>{% endfor %}</div></div></section>

